.TH HL 1
.SH NAME
hl \- tree-sitter's colors in acme's windows
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hl
[
.B -a
.I acme
] [
.B -s
.I astyles
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Hl
colors the text of
.IR acme (1)'s
windows by its syntax, as tree-sitter's grammars parse it,
in each window's
.IR astyles (4)
layer
.BR treesitter .
It waits for
.BR $acmesrv ,
an acme's
.B /srv
file, and follows its windows, mounted on
.I acme
.RB ( /mnt/acme ),
writing their layers in
.I astyles
.RB ( /mnt/astyles ).
.PP
A window whose file the first rule of
.B $home/lib/syn
or
.B /lib/syn
matches is colored by that rule's language, by its syntax program (see
.IR syn (4)).
.I Hl
gives a window's grammar its body once, under acme's
.B seq
guard, and then its edits, from the window's
.BR rdevent ,
and writes in its layer only the runs that the grammar says may have changed,
each under the
.B seq
of the edits it reflects, so that
.I astyles
refuses colors for text that has since changed,
and
.I hl
colors that text again after the next edits.
A Get, an edit whose text
.B rdevent
leaves out, or a grammar that has lost the document
has
.I hl
give the body again.
.PP
A language's program gives the text of a language it does not have,
such as a markdown file's fenced block of code, as one run,
.BI ts/ lang\f1,
or
.BI ts/ lang / name
for the run that the text takes when there is no program for
.IR lang .
.I Hl
gives that text to the program of the first rule with a
.B fence=
of
.IR lang ,
and puts the program's runs where the text is.
The program gets the block's edits as the window's program does,
and a block whose bounds an edit crosses is given again.
So a block marked
.B sh
is colored as
.BR bash .
.PP
.I Hl
starts each language's program once, by its rule's
.B cmd=
and
.IR rc (1),
and keeps it for every window in its language.
It sends a program the requests
.BR body ,
.BR insert ,
.BR delete ,
.B span
and
.B close
of
.IR syn (4).
A program's queries, in
.BR /sys/lib/ts ,
say what its runs are, and
.B /sys/lib/ts/names
the
.IR theme (6)
name each run takes.
.SH FILES
.TF /sys/lib/ts/names
.TP
.B /lib/syn
the languages' rules
.TP
.B /sys/lib/ts/names
capture names to
.IR theme (6)
names
.TP
.BI /bin/ts/ lang
a language's program
.PD
.SH SOURCE
plan9web's
.B src/cmd/hl.c
and
.B src/cmd/synrules.c
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR acme (1),
.IR Tree (1),
.IR astyles (4),
.IR syn (4),
.IR theme (6)
